    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: spatial_transitions\n---\n\n\n\n```python\nspatial_transitions(\n    data,\n    variable,\n    *,\n    w=None,\n    k=5,\n    m=None,\n    per_year=False,\n    relative=True,\n    title=None,\n    map=None,\n    gdf=None,\n    ref=None,\n)\n```\n\nSpatial Markov transitions: does a unit's mobility depend on where its neighbours stand?\n\nRey's spatial Markov chain splits the transition matrix of ``transitions`` by the\nclass of each unit's neighbours (their weighted mean), and tests whether the\nmatrices differ. Needs the ``[dynamics]`` extra.\n\n## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}\n\n| Name     | Type        | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | Default    |\n|----------|-------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|\n| data     |             | A dataset id, or a panel with ``geo_id`` and ``year``, e.g. from ``load``                                                                                                                                                                               | _required_ |\n| variable | str         | The numeric column to follow, observed in at least two years; the units without a value in every year are left out                                                                                                                                      | _required_ |\n| w        |             | Spatial weights from ``weights`` (default: queen contiguity among the units with data)                                                                                                                                                                  | `None`     |\n| k        | int         | Number of quantile classes of the variable                                                                                                                                                                                                              | `5`        |\n| m        | int \\| None | Number of quantile classes of the neighbours' mean (default: ``k``)                                                                                                                                                                                     | `None`     |\n| per_year | bool        | Classify each year on its own; by default all years are classified together, so classes are fixed levels                                                                                                                                                | `False`    |\n| relative | bool        | Divide the values by each year's mean first (default), so that classes are levels relative to the average unit; needs positive means                                                                                                                    | `True`     |\n| title    | str \\| None | The figure title                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | `None`     |\n| map      | str \\| None | The map (scale) the units are drawn on and their neighbours found, e.g. one of the project's municipal maps (default: the data's own map; needed only for a table whose units are on several maps and that does not record which, see ``geo.scales()``) | `None`     |\n| gdf      |             | Boundaries to use instead of the project's (a GeoDataFrame with ``geo_id``)                                                                                                                                                                             | `None`     |\n\n## Returns {.doc-section .doc-section-returns}\n\n| Name   | Type          | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n|--------|---------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n|        | result object | A result with ``.p_global`` (the transition probabilities of all units), ``.p_conditional`` (one matrix per class of the neighbours, from the lowest to the highest), ``.steady_states`` (the long-run distribution in each neighbourhood), ``.fig`` (the conditional matrices side by side), ``.gt`` (the tests of equal dynamics across neighbourhoods), ``.lr_stat``, ``.lr_p``, ``.q_stat``, ``.q_p``, ``.dof``, ``.df`` (one row per unit and year with its ``state`` and ``neighbor_state``) and ``.interpret()``. |\n\n## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}\n\n```python\n!pip install -q \"geo4bolivia[dynamics]\"\nimport geo4bolivia as geo\n\nres = geo.spatial_transitions(\"ntl\", \"ln_NTLpc\", k=5)\nprint(res.interpret())\nres.fig\n```\n\n\n::: {#e0961547 .cell execution_count=1}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\nThe spatial Markov chain splits **Log night-time lights per capita**'s 5-state transition matrix by the neighbors' position (spatial lag under queen contiguity (1 island(s) attached to nearest neighbor), row-standardized, n=322 (on map339)), giving one matrix per neighborhood class (5 classes); values were expressed relative to each year's mean first.\nThe unconditional matrix keeps units in place with average probability 0.832.\nConditioning on context, units surrounded by **low-value neighbors** stay in place with average probability 0.8, while units surrounded by **high-value neighbors** do so with 0.772 — movement is more common where the neighbors have high values.\nThe homogeneity tests (LR = 106, p = 6.65e-05; Q = 155, p = 3.04e-11; 56 degrees of freedom) are statistically significant at the 1% level: transition dynamics **differ across neighborhood contexts** — a unit's mobility is associated with the state of its neighbors.\n\n_These are associations, not causal effects. A causal reading needs a research design._\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:720px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5/tex-svg.min.js\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-4.1.1.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-O24V1F27f8pb0glCkelh3cVHLNiHAJ5gCaVtq2aNch8=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"b6e46929-87c9-4642-8c24-9a8e1ac21ff3\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};